WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.701
[music playing]

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.937
She's not even holding
an equilibrium there.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.807
Let's just give
her a few minutes.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.443
[water splashing lightly]

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.811
But she's definitely waking up.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.346
I think it's going to
be worth releasing.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.281
That's good.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.649
Send her up river.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.788
I'm glad we did that.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.056
She deserved it.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.023
[engine starting]

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.759
Well, let's go
check our other net.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.161
Maybe we can find a male
that we can eat tonight.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.768
There's definitely
debris in this one as well.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.070
Here we go again.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.505
Oh, here's one right here.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.506
Oh!

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.040
Looks like we're
catching fish.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.175
There he is.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:42.976
Think that's a male?

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:43.743
Yep.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.881
Something to eat.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.783
Oh, there's one here.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.652
We've got two nice ones there.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.021
That's payoff
for conservation.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:55.822
[chuckles]

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.893
I got something
heavy here, a live one.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.295
Oh, that's a big one.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.264
Oh, is that male?

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.398
Yeah.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.166
Yay.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:13.973
A little bit of driftwood
and three nice keeper fish.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.509
I'm glad that we don't
have a net full of fish

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.878
because that is more
than we would need.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:22.248
And we don't want to overfish.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.752
That's perfect for what
that species can give to us.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.691
Look who came.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.492
Hi--

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.293
Hi, Dickel.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.093
--Dickel.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.261
Yay.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.564
He says, you guys
cooking some salmon for me?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.466
Good boy, Dickel.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:43.770
Dickel's been a great
dog, and I think about all

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.773
the great times I had with
him, all the adventures

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.675
we've shared together.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.711
And I'd celebrate
that, not the fact

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.982
that it might be the last couple
of weeks or the last month.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.650
That is delicious.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.153
It's pretty hard to be
too much fresher than that.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.555
You know what I think
makes it really taste

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.458
good is knowing that
there is one that

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.294
was released out of it today.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.563
I'm very proud
of the fact that I

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.700
was able to release
a female king salmon

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.402
to go up and finish spawning.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:20.540
This life has provided a
really, really good life for me.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.109
And I just want other people
to have the opportunity

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.978
to experience that.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:25.778
Cheers.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.546
Cheers.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.081
[mimics clinking]

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.883
Oh, that's so good.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:30.950
[music playing]

